<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Dumnonia</h1><p class="st-meta">410 CE – 710 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Post-Roman British kingdom of Devon and Cornwall, with its high-status site at Tintagel, which slowly gave way to the West Saxons.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dumnonia grew from the Roman civitas of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dumnonii">Dumnonii</a> after Roman rule ended around 410, covering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devon">Devon</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a>. In the 6th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gildas">Gildas</a> denounced its king Constantine for murder and sacrilege. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britons-celtic-people">Britons</a> from the region emigrated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armorica">Armorica</a>, where the district of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/domnonee">Domnonée</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Brittany</a> carries the same name.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded of its government. Imported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> pottery and glass at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tintagel">Tintagel</a>, and at sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantham">Bantham</a>, show trade with the Byzantine world, probably for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a>, in the 5th and 6th centuries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> was organised around local saints and monasteries, and inscribed memorial stones in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and ogham mark the burials of its elite.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The West <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/saxons">Saxons</a> pushed westward through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devon">Devon</a> in the 7th century, and around 705 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aldhelm">Aldhelm</a> wrote to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geraint-of-dumnonia">Geraint</a> urging Roman practice on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-controversy">Easter</a>. In 710 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ine-of-wessex">Ine of Wessex</a> fought Geraint, and Devon was gradually absorbed. A smaller British kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a> survived until the 9th century.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 410 CE – 710 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:67.86%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>410 CE – 710 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Constantine, Geraint</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic, later Cornish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dumnonia, Domnonia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=560&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dumnonia" aria-label="Kingdom of Dumnonia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4600 417 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Dumnonia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4920 673L4920 673M4920 673L4970 663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4920 673h0M4970 663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4920 673h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4920 673h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=560&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dumnonia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
